<Project xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
	xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
	xmlns="http://usefulinc.com/ns/doap#">

	<name>Exmap Console</name>
	<shortname>exmap-console</shortname>
	<created>2006-12-01</created>

	<shortdesc xml:lang="en">Exmap-console is a command line frontend for Exmap.</shortdesc>

	<description xml:lang="en"> 

	Exmap-console is a suite of command line utilities developed around 
        John Berthels' Exmap tool for memory analysis (for more information 
        about Exmap see  http://www.berthels.co.uk/exmap). It is intended 
        primarily for use on embedded devices, where running the original 
        Exmap GUI is not feasible, or when it is necessary for other reasons 
        to save the data for later use.

	The suite contains three applications: an interactive gdb-like client, 
        daemon for automated data loging, and a remote server for remote
        analysis.

	</description>

